From 9eaefb80ed45fb2f2ee1b2b5b25d403e36f00266 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rustcc-build <rustcc@localhost>
Date: Sat, 9 May 2026 18:33:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.46-B4: hir::Class API + Adt::Class wired through hir/ide
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Brings the hir crate's user-facing API up to parity with Struct/Enum/Union for
class items, replacing the B.3 panic stubs in hir + hir-ty hot paths. The IDE
now hovers, navigates, completes, and infers on `class Foo {}` definitions.

Highlights:
- Define `hir::Class { id: ClassId }` with `name`/`module`/`fields`/`ty`/
  `visibility`/`kind`/`repr` mirrored from `hir::Struct`.
- Add `Adt::Class(Class)` and `Variant::Class(Class)` variants; replace all
  `unimplemented!` arms in `hir::from_id`, `hir::lib`, `hir::source_analyzer`,
  `hir::symbols`, `hir::semantics::child_by_source`, `hir::has_source`,
  `hir::display`, `hir::attrs`, and `hir::term_search::tactics` with real
  Class delegation that treats a class as a record-shaped struct.
- `ast::VariantDef` gains a `Class` arm; `ast::Adt::Class` is consumed by the
  hir source-mapping shim.
- New `SymbolKind::Class` (with semantic-token / LSP `CLASS` mappings, and a
  completion `cl` tag) so the IDE renders the keyword and picks a class icon
  while sharing record-shape behavior internally.
- Cascading fixes in ide / ide-assists / ide-completion / ide-db /
  ide-diagnostics / rust-analyzer (LSP layer, analysis-stats CLI) so the
  workspace is exhaustive over the new variants.
- hir-ty: extend `TyDefId` and `ValueTyDefId` to include `ClassId` (via
  `impl_from!`); add a Class arm to `AdtDef::new`, `AdtDef::Debug`, the
  `for_each_relevant_impl` module lookup, `lower::field_types_query`,
  `infer.rs`'s path-to-variant resolver, `infer/expr.rs`'s field lookup,
  `layout/adt.rs`, and the `next_solver::def_id::SolverDefId` debug printer.
- hir-def: add `keys::CLASS` dyn_map slot, and a class arm in the
  `field_attrs_query` walk that goes through CLASS_MEMBER_LIST::fields()
  directly (CLASS_MEMBER_LIST is not a RECORD_FIELD_LIST so it doesn't slot
  into `ast::FieldList`).

Out of scope, deferred:
- Method walking (B.4c). Class methods inside CLASS_MEMBER_LIST::methods()
  aren't wired into the inherent-impl machinery yet — that needs either a
  synthesized ImplId per class or extending ItemContainerId with a ClassId
  arm, both invasive enough to warrant their own patch. The smoke-test code
  exercising `d.legs()` / `d.speak()` therefore leaves the call types as
  `?ty: 1 (16%)` rather than panicking, which is the explicit B.4 success bar.
- Inheritance, `class Dog : Animal` (B.4b). Phase 1 parses the colon and the
  base PATH_TYPE is a direct child of CLASS, but wiring the base into method
  resolution / vtables requires changes to both ClassSignature and the
  inherent-impl chain. Deferred per the prompt's scope cut.

Smoke test (does NOT panic):
  echo 'class Animal { tag: u32, fn legs(&self) -> u32 { 4 } }
  class Dog : Animal { bark: u32, fn speak(&self) -> u32 { 1000 } }
  fn use_dog(d: Dog) -> u32 { d.legs() + d.speak() }' \
  > /tmp/rustcc-class-smoke/src/lib.rs
  target/release/rust-analyzer analysis-stats /tmp/rustcc-class-smoke
  # Inference: 91.77ms — runs cleanly, no `unimplemented!` panic.

Tests after the patch (unchanged from B.4a baseline):
  parser    315/0
  syntax     51/0
  hir-def   479/0
  hir-ty    969/0
  ide      1292/0
  ide-completion 727/0
  ide-db   196/0

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
